# Kiro skill artifacts (app-review, judgement, steering-maintenance)
**/.app-review/
**/.judgement/
**/.steering-maintenance/
# Workflow-agent scratch: plans, investigation reports and publish-pr run dirs
# written to <repo>/.agents/tasks/ by the agent sessions working on this repo.
# Not agent definitions — those live in the .kiro repo under .kiro/agents/.
**/.agents/

# Compiled Go binary (regenerated by `go build`); should not be committed.
/vibekit
# Local-dev Go workspace (resolves unpublished sibling modules via replace);
# never committed — CI builds from the published module proxy.
go.work
go.work.sum
node_modules/
static-src/node_modules/
static-src/node_modules/.vite/
static-src/node_modules/.vite-temp/
.vitest-cache/
# static/ holds a few hand-authored assets (index.html, manifest, icons) beside
# the bundler's output, and that output is JavaScript plus its sourcemaps. Ignore
# those by EXTENSION at any depth rather than by naming the directories the
# bundler emits today: the enumerated form left `static/exec-view/` uncovered for
# as long as that module existed, and every lazy chunk or generated module tree
# added next is another silent gap. There is no committed .js under static/; if
# one is ever needed, allow-list that file with a `!static/…` line here.
#
# Produced by `go run ./cmd/bundle` (esbuild: /app.js, hashed /chunks/, /sw.js,
# /style.css), by wiregen (/wire/*.gen.js), or fetched by the Dockerfile build
# stage (/vendor/). The binary embeds the built tree.
static/**/*.js
static/**/*.map
static/**/*.gz
static/chunks/
static/vendor/
static/style.css

# Stryker mutation-testing artifacts (weekly-stryker.yaml / local npx stryker run)
reports/
.stryker-tmp/
# `inPlace: true` runs Stryker in the real tree (see static-src/stryker.config.json),
# so the vitest-runner writes its per-worker setup files into static-src/ instead
# of into the sandbox, and nothing removes them afterwards.
static-src/stryker-setup-*.js

# Review/audit evidence notes (functional-review runs)
.audit/

# Byte-compiled Python from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
